# playpick cell: mode=walk boss=gorged (a coverage label only -- the walk
# starts at the door same as any other, same as every other mode=walk entry
# on [[#6]]) spec=druid:balance style=auto size=25 difficulty=heroic
# view=1280x800 save=carried (behaves as fresh per #273 -- the dev-server
# port is pid-derived so localStorage never actually carries across separate
# playbot invocations, so the unlock-hash recipe below is what actually
# reaches this cell).
#
# Checked sessions.jsonl and direction.md's hypothesis 6 first. The
# spire/westclimb/oratory/eastclimb door-destination mismatch (door log names
# one room, `crossed` event lands in a different one or nowhere) has three
# confirmations on record so far -- paladin:retribution/idle,
# druid:feral/good, rogue:assassination/auto-falls-back-to-good -- and every
# one of them is 10-normal, fresh save, desktop. Nobody has run that exact
# junction at 25-heroic, the hardest cell in the game, to see whether the
# mismatch is a property of the room-walking code (and so holds at any
# size/difficulty) or something specific to the normal-mode room layout.
# druid:balance is also a ranged caster -- the auto-fallback's parked-far-
# from-the-boss shape documented on this line so far (druid:feral melee under
# auto) has only ever been read on melee specs, never on a spec whose kit is
# built to be used at range.
#
# #b=marrow&s=25&h=1 unlocks the 25-heroic tier the same way every other
# 25-heroic carried-cell script in this ledger does, then backs out to the
# raid setup screen for size/difficulty/class exactly like
# playtest/plans/2026-09-29-17.play.

open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
tap back
tap raid
shot raid-setup
tap next
tap class:druid:balance
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start
targets
ui
evening auto 240 10
shot end
state
says
bill
